{"name":"Adobe Beige","hex":"#dcbfa6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adobe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An unburnt brick dried in the sun.","The earth from which such bricks are made."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adobe"},{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adobe","blocks":[{"text":"Adobe is a building material made from loam and organic materials. Adobe is Spanish for mudbrick. In some English-speaking regions of Spanish heritage, such as the Southwestern United States, the term is used to refer to any kind of earthen construction, or various architectural styles like Pueblo Revival or Territorial Revival. Most adobe buildings are similar in appearance to cob and rammed earth buildings. Adobe is among the earliest building materials, and is used throughout the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg/330px-Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe","wikidata":"Q183496"},{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where the word originally meant natural wool that has been neither bleached nor dyed, hence also the color of natural wool."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg/330px-Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beige","wikidata":"Q843607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg/500px-AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg/500px-AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Renewal of the surface coating of an adobe wall in Chamisal, New Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Qasroddasht.JPG/500px-Qasroddasht.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Qasroddasht.JPG/1280px-Qasroddasht.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Qasroddasht.JPG/500px-Qasroddasht.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adobe walls separate urban gardens in Shiraz, Iran","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQasroddasht.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/San_Pedro_de_Atacama_church.jpg/500px-San_Pedro_de_Atacama_church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/San_Pedro_de_Atacama_church.jpg/1280px-San_Pedro_de_Atacama_church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/San_Pedro_de_Atacama_church.jpg/500px-San_Pedro_de_Atacama_church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp